.TH GIRL 1 2026-10-09 girlpages "girlpages Manual"
.SH NAME
girl \- an interface to the system reference manuals, but make it girly
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B girl
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ section ]
.IR page \ ...
.br
.B girl
.B \-k
.IR regexp \ ...
.br
.B girl
.B \-f
.IR page \ ...
.br
.B girl
.B \-\-bulk
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ section \ ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B girl
works like
.BR man (1):
it finds the manual page you ask for and shows it in a pager.
The difference is that the page is first rewritten by a large language model
in the voice of a Gen Z teenage girl, with colour and emoji, while keeping
every option, argument, default, file, example and caveat of the original.
.PP
Pages are found with
.BR "man \-w" ,
so names, sections and search order behave exactly as they do for
.BR man .
The page is rendered to plain text with
.BR man ,
sent to the model, and the result is stored in a cache.
If a page is already cached it is shown straight away without contacting the
model; this includes pages whose source has since changed, which are shown
with a note until they are refreshed.
.PP
Identical pages (such as aliases made with symbolic links or
.B .so
requests) share one conversion.
Long pages are split at section boundaries and converted in parts.
If the model leaves out any command-line options that appear in the original,
the part is retried once with a list of what went missing.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Options shared with man"
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Show every matching page, not just the first.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-S ", " \-\-sections =\fIlist\fR
Only search the given sections, separated by colons or commas.
A section can also be given as the first argument, as in
.BR "girl 3 printf" .
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-apropos
Search page names and descriptions.
This runs
.B man \-k
directly.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-whatis
Show one-line descriptions.
This runs
.B man \-f
directly.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-where ", " \-\-path ", " \-\-location
Print the location of the source pages instead of showing them.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-local\-file
Treat each argument as a man page file rather than a page name.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-manpath =\fIpath\fR
Search
.I path
instead of the default manual path.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-locale =\fIlocale\fR
Look for pages in this locale.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-pager =\fIpager\fR
Use
.I pager
to display output.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-config\-file =\fIfile\fR
Read
.I file
instead of the user configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SS "Display options"
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Convert the page again even if it is cached, replacing the cached copy.
.TP
.B \-\-cached\-only
Never contact the model; fail for pages that are not cached.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Print the stored markup instead of rendering it.
.TP
.BR \-\-color =\fIwhen\fR
Use colour
.BR always ,
.BR never ,
or
.B auto
(the default), which uses colour when standard output is a terminal and
.B NO_COLOR
is not set.
.TP
.BR \-\-backend =\fIname\fR
Use the
.BR auto ,
.BR openai ,
or
.B claude
backend, overriding the configuration.
.TP
.BR \-\-model =\fImodel\fR
Ask this model, overriding the configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Show which configuration files were read, which backend and model will be
used, and what each cache holds.
.SS "Bulk options"
.TP
.B \-\-bulk
Convert every page in the manual path (the top-level
.BI man N
directories; translations are skipped), most useful sections first.
Pages that are already cached and unchanged are skipped, so running it again
only does new work.
Sections may be given as arguments, as in
.BR "girl \-\-bulk 1 8" .
After a complete run without section or limit filters,
.B \-\-update
runs also convert new pages.
.TP
.B \-\-update
Refresh pages whose source has changed since they were converted.
If a complete
.B \-\-bulk
run has been done in this cache before, new pages are converted too;
otherwise only pages that are already cached are looked at.
This is what the package-manager hooks and timers run.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Convert pages even if they are up to date.
.TP
.B \-\-prune
After a complete run, remove cache entries for pages that no longer exist and
conversions that nothing refers to.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
List the pages that would be converted, and convert nothing.
No backend is needed.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs =\fIn\fR
Send up to
.I n
requests to the model at once.
.TP
.BR \-\-limit =\fIn\fR
Only look at the first
.I n
pages.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Only report errors.
.SH BACKENDS
.SS claude
Runs the
.BR claude (1)
command-line tool in print mode:
.PP
.RS
.nf
claude \-p \-\-output\-format text \-\-no\-session\-persistence \e
    \-\-system\-prompt \fIprompt\fR \-\-tools "" \-\-strict\-mcp\-config \e
    \-\-disable\-slash\-commands \-\-setting\-sources "" [\-\-model \fImodel\fR]
.fi
.RE
.PP
with the page on standard input, from the temporary directory, so that the
user's own MCP servers, skills, hooks and project files stay out of it.
.SS openai
Posts to the
.B /chat/completions
endpoint of any OpenAI-compatible API, such as OpenAI, OpenRouter, Ollama,
llama.cpp, vLLM or LM Studio.
Rate-limited and failed requests are retried.
.SS auto
The default.
Uses
.B openai
if
.B openai.base_url
is set to something other than OpenAI's own endpoint, otherwise
.B claude
if the command is on
.BR PATH ,
otherwise
.B openai
if an API key is configured.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from the system configuration file, then the user
configuration file (or the file given with
.BR \-C ),
then the environment, with later sources winning.
The files are in TOML:
.PP
.RS
.nf
backend = "auto"         # auto, openai or claude
jobs = 4                 # requests at once
chunk_size = 12000       # bytes of text per request
cache_dir = ""           # where to write conversions
pager = ""
extra_instructions = ""  # appended to the prompt

[claude]
command = "claude"
model = "sonnet"
args = []
timeout = "15m"

[openai]
base_url = "https://api.openai.com/v1"
model = ""
api_key = ""
api_key_file = ""
temperature = 0.9
max_tokens = 16000
timeout = "10m"

[openai.headers]
"X\-Example" = "value"
.fi
.RE
.PP
A system configuration file that holds an API key should not be world-readable;
use
.B api_key_file
pointing at a file only root can read, and users will still see every page the
system cache already has.
.SH CACHE
Conversions are stored as
.BI objects/ xx / sha256 .girl
files named by the hash of the plain-text page, with an index under
.B index/
that maps each source file to its conversion and records the source's size and
modification time.
.PP
.B girl
reads the cache it writes to and the system cache.
It writes to
.B cache_dir
if that is set, to the system cache when run as root, and to the user's cache
otherwise.
When the same page is in both, an up-to-date copy is preferred.
.SH "PACKAGE MANAGER HOOKS"
A system-wide install adds a hook for each package manager it finds:
an apt
.B DPkg::Post\-Invoke
hook, a pacman hook on
.BR usr/share/man/* ,
and a dnf post-transaction action.
Each runs
.BR girlpages\-hook ,
which starts
.B girlpages\-update.service
(or, without systemd, a background
.BR "girl \-\-bulk \-\-update \-\-prune" )
and never fails the transaction.
A daily
.B girlpages\-update.timer
catches pages installed any other way.
A per-user install gets the same timer as a user unit.
.PP
Since
.B \-\-update
only converts new pages after a complete
.B \-\-bulk
run, the hooks cost nothing until an administrator opts in with
.BR "sudo girl \-\-bulk" .
.PP
The service runs as root.
When using the
.B claude
backend, root's
.B claude
must be logged in, or point
.B claude.command
at a wrapper.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GIRLPAGER
Pager to use; checked before
.BR PAGER .
.B MANPAGER
is not used, as it often removes formatting.
.TP
.B PAGER
Pager to use if
.B GIRLPAGER
is not set.
The default is
.BR less ,
which is given
.B \-R
so colours come through.
.TP
.B MANWIDTH
Width to lay pages out at.
Otherwise the terminal width is used, up to 100 columns.
.TP
.B MANPATH
As for
.BR man .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off.
.TP
.B GIRLPAGES_CONFIG
User configuration file to read.
.TP
.BR GIRLPAGES_BACKEND ", " GIRLPAGES_MODEL ", " GIRLPAGES_JOBS ", " GIRLPAGES_CACHE_DIR
Override
.BR backend ,
the model,
.B jobs
and
.BR cache_dir .
.TP
.BR GIRLPAGES_OPENAI_BASE_URL ", " OPENAI_BASE_URL
Override
.BR openai.base_url .
.TP
.BR GIRLPAGES_OPENAI_API_KEY ", " OPENAI_API_KEY
Override
.BR openai.api_key .
.TP
.BR GIRLPAGES_OPENAI_MODEL ", " GIRLPAGES_CLAUDE_MODEL ", " GIRLPAGES_CLAUDE_COMMAND
Override the per-backend settings.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_CACHE_HOME
Locate the user configuration file and cache.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/girlpages/config.toml
System configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/girlpages/config.toml
User configuration.
.TP
.I /var/cache/girlpages
System cache.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/girlpages
User cache.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage or configuration error.
.TP
.B 2
A page could not be converted, or a bulk run had failures.
.TP
.B 16
A page was not found.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B girl ls
Show
.BR ls (1).
.TP
.B girl 3 printf
Show
.BR printf (3)
rather than
.BR printf (1).
.TP
.B girl \-\-refresh \-\-model opus tar
Convert
.BR tar (1)
again with a different model.
.TP
.B sudo girl \-\-bulk \-j 8 1 8
Convert every page in sections 1 and 8 into the system cache, eight at a time.
.TP
.B girl \-\-bulk \-\-dry\-run
See how many pages a full run would convert.
.SH BUGS
The model can still get things wrong.
When something matters, check the original with
.BR man .
.PP
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/NaomiAmethyst/girlpages/issues
.UE .
